\smallskip
\State \hskip4em 2) Process $p_i$ proposes $v_1$ to $\mathcal{A}^S$. Process $p_i$ runs (i.e., simulates) $\mathcal{A}^S$ in the following way: (1) $p_i$ executes $\mathcal{A}^S$ for exactly $\mathcal{R}$ rounds, (2) \hphantom{aaaaaaaaaaa}each round lasts for exactly $\Delta_{\mathit{sync}}$ time, and (3) $p_i$ does not send more than $\mathcal{B}$ bits.
